{"name":"Chert","hex":"#848182","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chert","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Massive, usually dull-colored and opaque, quartzite, hornstone, impure chalcedony, or other flint-like mineral.","A flint-like tool made from chert."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chert"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chert","blocks":[{"text":"Chert is a hard, fine-grained sedimentary rock composed of microcrystalline or cryptocrystalline quartz, the mineral form of silicon dioxide (SiO2). Chert is characteristically of biological origin, but may also occur inorganically as a chemical precipitate or a diagenetic replacement, as in petrified wood. Where chert occurs in chalk or marl, it is usually called flint."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/ChertUSGOV.jpg/330px-ChertUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chert"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Chert_beds_EverettPA.jpg/500px-Chert_beds_EverettPA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Chert_beds_EverettPA.jpg/500px-Chert_beds_EverettPA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chert (dark bands) in the Devonian Corriganville-New Creek limestone, Everett, Pennsylvania","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChert_beds_EverettPA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Folded_layers_of_bedded_chert_formation_in_Busuanga%2C_Palawan_02.jpg/500px-Folded_layers_of_bedded_chert_formation_in_Busuanga%2C_Palawan_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Folded_layers_of_bedded_chert_formation_in_Busuanga%2C_Palawan_02.jpg/1280px-Folded_layers_of